# Nothing here is content-hashed — the app is /app.js and /styles.css, by
# those names, forever. Without this a browser is free to keep a copy for as
# long as it likes, and Safari in particular will: a Mac showed a layout
# several deploys old while the server had been serving the new one for days.
#
# `no-cache` does not mean "do not store". It means "revalidate before use",
# so the browser still keeps the file and still gets a 304 with an empty body
# when nothing has changed. The cost is one conditional request per file per
# load; the alternative is people silently running old code.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
